Hi!

TimeBrowse v0.6 is released!
http://sourceforge.net/projects/timebrowse/

With v0.6,  evince and pisa dependency are removed.  Therefore natty
users are supposed to use the TimeBrowse extension without any changes.
The extenstion also supports scaleble thumbnail by draging pane window
and drag and drop for restoring the history.

snapshot manager includes init and upsart scripts.  So it can be easily
used just like regular daemon starting on boot time.

Changes are following.

TimeBrowse-v0.6  Wed Mar 30 19:35:17 JST 2011
        * drag and drop
        * scalable thumbnail functionality
        * remove evince/pisa dependency to create thumbnail
        * fix confusing prompt in confirm dialog (Ryusuke Konishi)

nilfs2_ss_manager-v0.6  Wed Mar 30 19:35:17 JST 2011
        * ignore already unmounted mountpoint (Ryusuke Konishi)
        * add pidfile option (Ryusuke Konishi)
        * add log priority configuration (Ryusuke Konishi)
        * add verbose option (Ryusuke Konishi)
        * add init script and default file (Ryusuke Konishi)
        * add upstart script (Ryusuke Konishi)

enjoy!
